hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19564","Muawiyah ibn Abdillah ibn Muawiyah ibn Asim ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir al-Qari narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from al-Shabi or Khaythamah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the Muslims is like one man; when something of him aches, the rest of his body sympathizes with him."
"19565","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Waki al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from al-Shabi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the minbar: Whoever does not thank little will not thank much, and whoever does not thank people will not thank Allah. Speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude. Unity is mercy and division is punishment."
"19566","Abdullah said: Yahya ibn Abd Rabbihi, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me, Abu Waki narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from al-Shabi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on these sticks, or on this minbar: Whoever does not thank little will not thank much, and whoever does not thank people will not thank Allah. Speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude. Unity is mercy and division is punishment. He said: Abu Umamah al-Bahili said: Stick to the great majority. He said: A man said: What is the great majority. Abu Umamah called out this verse in Surat al-Nur: If they turn away, upon him is what he was charged with and upon you is what you were charged with."
"19567","Abdillah ibn Umar, he is al-Qawariri, narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn al-Muhallab, narrated to us, from his father, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Treat your children equitably, meaning: make them equal."
"19568","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Bahili and Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told me, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal ibn al-Muhallab, from his father, that he heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be just among your children, be just among your children."
